From 164c33700e48de0189a83f2c7b8fed549c8d5dfe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abdulaziz <alanziabdulaziz4@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 10:28:24 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] ggml-cpu: AVX2/AVX-VNNI kernels for PQ2_0 + Q8_K activations
 + tiled GEMM (x86 without AVX-512)

The fork's fast PQ2_0 paths (gemv/gemm_pq2_0_4x8) are gated on AVX-512, so 12th-14th gen Intel and other AVX2/AVX-VNNI CPUs fell back to
the generic scalar dot. This adds:

- ggml_vec_dot_pq2_0_q8_0 / ggml_vec_dot_pq2_0_q8_K (AVX2, AVX-VNNI, AVX-512VNNI-VL): 2-bit codes unpacked with srlv+and, dpbusd
  against the permuted activation bytes, unsigned-code correction via a lane-wise sum(y) so per-lane partials stay exact.
- PQ2_0 vec_dot_type switched to Q8_K (one activation scale per 256): 4 dpbusd + 1 sub + 1 cvt + 1 fmadd per 128 weights instead of
  4x(2 dpbusd + sub + cvt + fmadd). Perplexity unchanged within 0.004 (Bonsai-2 27B: 7.0542 -> 7.0583 +/- 0.58).
- llamafile/sgemm.cpp: tinyBLAS_PQ2K_AVX / tinyBLAS_PQ2_AVX tiled GEMMs. A 128-weight block is unpacked once per row tile and reused
  across RN token columns; the activation permute and lane sums are staged once per matmul call per thread; jobs are row tiles
  (each weight row streams from DRAM exactly once) claimed dynamically from the threadpool counter in runs of 8 so P- and E-cores
  share the compute-bound loop. Float accumulation order and reduction are identical to the vec_dot path, so batched and
  single-token results are bit-identical (PPL identical with PQ2_SGEMM=0/1).

Measured on an i7-13620H (6P+4E, AVX2+AVX-VNNI, single-channel DDR5-5200 ~28 GB/s effective), Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B PQ2_0:
  decode (N=1)            1.3 -> 3.9-4.2 tok/s (generic -> vec_dot)
  batch cost, ms/token    N=4: 123 -> 78, N=8: 99 -> 68, N=16: 89 -> 54 (t=12, 65 W), N=64: 89 -> 69
  prompt processing       6.7 -> 16 tok/s
  MTP speculative verify (N=3) becomes ~1 DRAM sweep, giving 6.8-8.3 tok/s greedy decode with the grafted nextn head.
Env: PQ2_SGEMM=0 disables the tiled path (A/B).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QrdPnP5KL449GsoWBZx52R
